# React & TypeScript Patterns

> **Note**: These patterns reflect current frontend architecture. Adapt as React patterns evolve or project needs change.

## Component Structure

- Use functional components with hooks (React 19 patterns)
- Extract reusable logic into custom hooks (e.g., `useUrlDrivenSearch`)
- Keep pure logic in `lib/` modules (no React imports) for testability
- Route-level components go in `pages/`
- Reusable UI components go in `components/`

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD: Custom hook for URL-driven state
export function useUrlDrivenSearch<T>(
  paramKey: string,
  defaultValue: T,
  parseFn: (value: string) => T | null
): [T, (value: T) => void] {
  // ...
}

// ✅ GOOD: Pure logic module (no React imports)
export function canonicalRadius(radius: number): number {
  // Pure function, no dependencies
}
```

## API Client

- Use `api/client.ts` for all API calls
- Support `AbortSignal` for request cancellation
- Handle errors consistently with typed error responses
- Use environment variable `VITE_API_URL` for API base URL

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD: API client with abort support
export async function geocode(
  query: string,
  signal?: AbortSignal
): Promise<GeocodeResponse> {
  const response = await fetch(`${API_BASE_URL}/geocode?q=${encodeURIComponent(query)}`, {
    signal,
  });
  if (!response.ok) {
    const error = await response.json();
    throw new ApiError(error.code, error.message, error.details);
  }
  return response.json();
}
```

## URL Parameter Handling

- Parse and validate URL parameters in `lib/` modules (`exploreParams.ts`, `compareParams.ts`)
- Use shared radius constants from `radiusParams.ts`
- Validate parameters match API constraints (e.g., radius 0.1-3.0 miles)

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD: URL param parsing with validation
export function parseExploreParams(searchParams: URLSearchParams): ExploreParams | null {
  const radius = parseRadius(searchParams.get('radius'));
  if (!radius || radius < MIN_RADIUS || radius > MAX_RADIUS) {
    return null;
  }
  // ...
}
```

## TypeScript Types

- Define API response types in `types/api.ts`
- Use strict type checking (`npx tsc --noEmit`)
- Handle nullable/optional types explicitly

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD: Explicit API types
export interface GeocodeResponse {
  lat: number;
  lon: number;
  label: string;
}

export interface WalkabilitySummary {
  geoid20: string;
  d2a_ranked: number;
  // ...
}
```

## Leaflet Integration

- Use Leaflet directly via imperative API (not React-Leaflet wrapper)
- Create maps in `useEffect` hooks, manage lifecycle with refs
- Center maps on geocoded coordinates
- Display radius buffers as circles
- Render block group geometries from API responses as GeoJSON layers
- Clean up map instances on component unmount to prevent memory leaks

## Testing

- Use Vitest + React Testing Library for unit tests
- Use Playwright for E2E tests
- Test hooks, components, and pure logic modules separately
- Run `npx tsc --noEmit && npm run lint` before marking work complete
